    {
      "id": "table-13",
      "line": 308,
      "heading_context": "## Common Confusion Points",
      "headers": [
        "Confusion",
        "Correction"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "\"rustc owns the standard library.\"",
          "No. libs/libs-api own the public library API; rustc and std co-evolve."
        ],
        [
          "\"`std` is Rust's runtime.\"",
          "No. It is a statically linked library facade over `core`, `alloc`, and OS APIs."
        ],
        [
          "\"`no_std` means no Rust standard semantics.\"",
          "No. You still have `core`, traits, `Option`, `Result`, slices, and iterators."
        ],
        [
          "\"`alloc` requires an operating system.\"",
          "No. It requires a heap allocator, not necessarily hosted OS services."
        ],
        [
          "\"Lang items are a stable extension point.\"",
          "No. They are compiler/library implementation details."
        ],
        [
          "\"Panic unwind is just exceptions.\"",
          "Only mechanically similar in stack unwinding; Rust uses `Result` for expected errors."
        ],
        [
          "\"All targets have `std`.\"",
          "No. Some targets support only `core` or `core` + `alloc`; target tier matters."
        ]
      ]
    },
